{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdufiUgasjEZscnNv9iWQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed and committed.\n\n**The bug:** `median()` in `src/stats.py:20-21` only ever returned `ordered[mid]` — the upper middle element — with no even-length branch at all. `median([1, 2, 3, 4])` returned `3` instead of `2.5`.\n\n**The fix:** added the even-length case, averaging the two middle elements:\n\n```python\nmid = len(ordered) // 2\nif len(ordered) % 2 == 0:\n    return (ordered[mid - 1] + ordered[mid]) / 2\nreturn ordered[mid]\n```\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` now passes all 3 tests. Tests were not modified; the change is committed as `c80f297`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":26412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":228},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d0979c1-b259-438f-aa68-47b1c96f97a3","uuid":"bc535eb0-456c-4f91-9d85-0ef94b5d5b0a","timestamp":"2026-08-10T20:05:09.255Z","request_id":"req_011CdufiSwQuxYytqnN3TwXK"}
